nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"The movie is romantic or the movie is romantic, or the movie is comic.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"The movie is romantic or the movie is romantic\" to just \"The movie is romantic.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The movie is romantic, or the movie is comic.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely as\n\n\"The movie is romantic or comic.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380249 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157239 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "857d696d-6a3f-5fff-a5e1-b05148f28f55" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Sentences Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfe5cf7b-34eb-579b-9de5-66399500f2a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The actor is talented or successful" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380251} {:answer/id #uuid "30244b4c-438e-5366-9917-43241c71cfc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The actor is talented" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380252} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a60427-f52c-5b3a-ae20-3a29782bff43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The actor is talented but not successful" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380253} {:answer/id #uuid "e604e0e4-76fa-58b1-8eb9-2a0132713d34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The actor is successful" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380254} {:answer/id #uuid "3723d2e4-7af5-507a-8e12-579bed0e2c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The actor is talented and successful" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3723d2e4-7af5-507a-8e12-579bed0e2c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The actor is talented and successful" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380255} :answer-field/id #uuid "abb97ba1-9dda-568d-8499-4d801e4f661c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f240e16-b06d-50d1-bdc6-1009b836ca04" :question/math-academy-id "q-89254" :question/problem "Simplify the following sentence: \"The actor is talented and the actor is successful, and the actor is successful or is a successful actor.\"" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify the phrase \"the actor is successful or is a successful actor\" to just \"the actor is successful.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The actor is talented and the actor is successful, and the actor is successful.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"The actor is talented, and the actor is successful and the actor is successful.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"the actor is successful and the actor is successful\" to just \"the actor is successful.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The actor is talented, and the actor is successful.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"The actor is talented and successful.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "331fa12f-a113-5aba-bd6e-5bd5bf62298f" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Symbolic Statements Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41602012-bb04-5534-99d3-1c336df87d22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394822} {:answer/id #uuid "d42d1bd4-4961-5827-8390-3da0a398ab43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394823} {:answer/id #uuid "02b88ca0-c86b-513b-804e-f3b44341424b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394824} {:answer/id #uuid "e43ee3bb-80df-5c31-80d1-c1a57e26a965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394825} {:answer/id #uuid "662d7345-9f00-55a6-9a0c-dea7cf22c9c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "662d7345-9f00-55a6-9a0c-dea7cf22c9c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394826} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bd8780b-5e12-55d9-bb80-be017170c855" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8088540-0f2b-5602-b820-b1ed9dad2fb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-89266" :question/problem "Simplify $(P∨Q)∨(Q∧Q).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the associative and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∨(Q∧Q) & ≡(P∨Q)∨Q \\\\  & ≡P∨(Q∨Q) \\\\  & ≡P∨Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
